#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: FENECON Home"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The FENECON Home is a home storage system consisting of a hybrid inverter, "
"battery and energy management. This page summarizes what the **OpenEMS "
"source code** contains about the FENECON Home: structure, settings, "
"protective functions and additional functions. FENECON devices run the "
"manufacturer's own FEMS; individual functions may differ there or be "
"available earlier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Models"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-models
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS has the following Home variants, each as a separate app in the app "
"center:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Model\n"
"| App\n"
"| Inverter (according to the code)\n"
"| Series\n"
"| DC PV inputs (MPPT)\n"
"\n"
"| FENECON Home 10\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home\n"
"| FENECON FHI 10 DAH\n"
"| ET\n"
"| 2\n"
"| FENECON Home 6\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home6\n"
"| FENECON ET Gen2 6K\n"
"| EUB\n"
"| 2\n"
"| FENECON Home 10 Gen2\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home10.Gen2\n"
"| FENECON ET Gen2 10K\n"
"| EUB\n"
"| 3\n"
"| FENECON Home 15\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home15\n"
"| FENECON ET Gen2 15K\n"
"| EUB\n"
"| 3\n"
"| FENECON Home 20\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home.20\n"
"| FENECON FHI 20 DAH\n"
"| ETT\n"
"| 2\n"
"| FENECON Home 30\n"
"| App.FENECON.Home.30\n"
"| FENECON FHI 30 DAH (internally 29.9 kW)\n"
"| ETT\n"
"| 3\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"Technically, the inverters come from the GoodWe family. In the code, the "
"series are called “ET” (Home 10), “ETT – Home Series 20 & 30 kW” and “EUB – "
"Home Gen2 Series 6, 10 & 15 kW”. The inverter type is recognized by the "
"serial number. The Home apps may only be seen and deleted by installers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**DC inputs on Home 20 and 30:** Previously, the individual PV strings were "
"entered there (Home 20: 4 strings, Home 30: 6 strings, i.e. 2 strings per "
"MPPT). This division is marked as “no longer supported” in the code and is "
"only displayed for existing systems. New entries are made per MPPT input: 2 "
"for the Home 20, 3 for the Home 30."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generations"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-generations
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"Two generations are commonly distinguished: **generation 1** is the Home 10 "
"with 2.2 kWh battery modules, **generation 2** are the Home 6, 10 Gen2, 15, "
"20 and 30 with 2.8 kWh modules. The OpenEMS code does not use this "
"classification in this way. It distinguishes by **inverter series** and "
"**battery module type**. This results in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| \n"
"| Home 10 (Gen 1)\n"
"| Home 6 / 10 Gen2 / 15\n"
"| Home 20 / 30\n"
"\n"
"| Inverter series\n"
"| ET\n"
"| EUB (“Home Gen2”)\n"
"| ETT\n"
"| Permitted battery modules\n"
"| only 52 Ah (2.2 kWh)\n"
"| 52 Ah (2.2 kWh) **or** 64.4 Ah (2.8 kWh)\n"
"| only 64.4 Ah (2.8 kWh)\n"
"| Max. battery current\n"
"| 25 A\n"
"| 25 A with 52 Ah modules, 40 A with 64.4 Ah modules\n"
"| 50 A\n"
"| Max. battery charging power\n"
"| 10 kW\n"
"| 9 / 16 / 24 kW\n"
"| 20 / 30 kW\n"
"| Max. battery discharging power\n"
"| 10 kW\n"
"| 6.6 / 11 / 16.5 kW\n"
"| 20 / 30 kW\n"
"| DC PV inputs (MPPT)\n"
"| 2\n"
"| 2 / 3 / 3\n"
"| 2 / 3\n"
"| Grid meter\n"
"| Home 3-phase sensor (fixed)\n"
"| integrated sensor or external sensor (120 A) or sensor with own current transformers\n"
"| external sensor (120 A) or sensor with own current transformers\n"
"| Additional AC meter (for AC PV)\n"
"| yes\n"
"| no\n"
"| yes\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Important:** According to the code, the Home 6, 10 Gen2 and 15 may also be "
"operated with the older 2.2 kWh modules, but then with lower battery current "
"(25 instead of 40 A). The equation “Gen2 = 2.8 kWh modules” therefore only "
"applies to the Home 20 and 30 in the code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Impermissible combination"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-impermissible-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS checks whether the inverter and battery modules match. If the "
"combination is not permitted, for example a Home 10 inverter (Gen 1) with "
"2.8 kWh modules or a Home 20/30 with 2.2 kWh modules, then:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-impermissible-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "**charging and discharging are blocked** (battery current 0 A),"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-impermissible-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"the warning appears: “The installed inverter and battery combination is not "
"authorised. Operation could cause hardware damages, so charging and "
"discharging is blocked. Please install a complete Home 10, Home 20 or Home "
"30 system.”"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-impermissible-combination
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS reads the module type from the battery management. With very old "
"battery firmware that does not report the type, 52 Ah (2.2 kWh) is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control computer generations (do not confuse)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-computer-generations-do-not-confuse
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"In the code, “Gen2” and “Gen3” also appear for the **control computer** "
"(compute module “CM4S Gen2” or “CM4S Gen3”). This is independent of the Home "
"generation. The following depend on it, for example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-computer-generations-do-not-confuse
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"the relay used to start the battery (`+io0/Relay6+` for CM4S Gen3, otherwise "
"`+io0/Relay4+`),"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-computer-generations-do-not-confuse
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "whether an additional relay board is set up,"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-computer-generations-do-not-confuse
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "the status LED and the § 14a limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure in OpenEMS"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-in-openems
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"When a Home app is installed, it automatically sets up these building blocks:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Building block\n"
"| typical ID\n"
"| Task\n"
"\n"
"| Battery\n"
"| battery0\n"
"| Battery management (BMS) of the FENECON Home battery tower\n"
"| Battery inverter\n"
"| batteryInverter0\n"
"| Hybrid inverter\n"
"| Storage system\n"
"| ess0\n"
"| combines battery and inverter into one controllable storage system\n"
"| Grid meter\n"
"| meter0\n"
"| 3-phase sensor at the house connection\n"
"| PV inputs (DC)\n"
"| charger0, charger1 …\n"
"| Solar modules directly on the inverter (MPPT)\n"
"| Emergency power meter\n"
"| meter2\n"
"| measures the emergency power output (if available)\n"
"| Relay board\n"
"| io0\n"
"| among other things, start relay of the battery\n"
"| Communication\n"
"| modbus0, modbus1, modbus2\n"
"| internal connections to battery and inverter, possibly external meters\n"
"| Emergency reserve\n"
"| ctrlEmergencyCapacityReserve0\n"
"| keeps capacity free for power outages\n"
"| DC surplus feed-in\n"
"| ctrlEssSurplusFeedToGrid0\n"
"| feeds DC surplus into the grid if the battery cannot absorb it\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition, matching apps are installed or required: self-consumption "
"optimization, xref:user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc[grid-"
"optimized charge], xref:user/schedule/forecasts.adoc[forecasts], depending "
"on the hardware the status LED and possibly a limitation according to § 14a "
"EnWG."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Settings during installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Country and grid"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Country setting\n"
"| Country's grid regulations for the inverter: Germany, Austria, Switzerland, Sweden, Czech Republic, Netherlands, Greece, Lithuania, etc.\n"
"| Grid setting\n"
"| Reactive power behavior: Q(U) curve, P(U) curve, fixed cos φ = 1 or fixed cos φ between 0.80 and 0.99 (inductive or capacitive)\n"
"| Remote shutdown (central grid and system protection)\n"
"| Shutdown by an external grid and system protection\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed-in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Type of limitation\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| No limitation\n"
"| no limitation of feed-in\n"
"| Dynamic feed-in\n"
"| The feed-in at the grid connection is limited to a fixed value (e.g. 60 % or 70 % of the PV power); OpenEMS controls the inverter for this.\n"
"| Ripple control receiver\n"
"| The grid operator limits via ripple control receiver.\n"
"| Dynamic ripple control receiver\n"
"| Ripple control receiver whose specifications OpenEMS implements dynamically\n"
"| Dynamic feed-in & ripple control receiver\n"
"| both combined\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The maximum feed-in power is stored centrally in the system settings and can "
"also be changed there later (“Feed-In Settings”). This value is additionally "
"limited by the fusing of the grid connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meters"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-meters
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Grid meter:** Home 3-phase sensor with 120 A current transformer (default) "
"or without current transformer. On Gen2 models, the sensor is integrated; an "
"external one is optional. With current transformers, the primary current is "
"entered (200 to 5000 A, secondary 5 A)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-meters
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**AC meter** (Home 10, 20, 30): optional meter for an additional AC-coupled "
"PV system (Socomec or KDK type)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "PV"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pv
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**DC PV inputs:** Which inputs (MPPT) are occupied; each can be given its "
"own name."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pv
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Shadow management:** The inverter regularly searches for the best "
"operating point when modules are partially shaded. **It only has to be "
"deactivated if power optimizers are installed on the modules.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Emergency power"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-emergency-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Activate emergency power supply**: whether an emergency power output is "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-emergency-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Emergency reserve**: Part of the battery is not discharged during normal "
"operation so that it is available in the event of a power failure. "
"Adjustable from 5 to 100 %, default 10 %."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-other
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**§ 14a EnWG:** If a control device of the grid operator is connected, the "
"storage power can be limited on its instructions (depending on the hardware)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Battery"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-battery
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The battery tower consists of modules; several towers are possible. OpenEMS "
"automatically recognizes the module type:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module type\n"
"| Capacity per module\n"
"| Cells per module\n"
"| Initial maximum current\n"
"\n"
"| 52 Ah\n"
"| 2.2 kWh\n"
"| 14\n"
"| 40 A\n"
"| 64.4 Ah\n"
"| 2.8 kWh\n"
"| 14\n"
"| 50 A\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The storage capacity results from the number of modules. Voltage and "
"temperature are monitored **per tower and module**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"In detail on the battery (BMS communication, charging and discharging "
"limits, emergency reserve, startup and shutdown): xref:user/systems/fenecon-"
"home-battery.adoc[FENECON Home battery]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protective functions"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-protective-functions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Charging and discharging current** are limited depending on cell voltage "
"and temperature. After a limitation, the current is only increased slowly "
"again (0.1 A per second)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-protective-functions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Deep discharge protection:** If the cell voltage falls too low (critical "
"limit 2.8 V), OpenEMS reports in stages (see table)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-protective-functions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"At very low state of charge, the battery can be force-charged with a small "
"current (2 A per tower)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Messages at low cell voltage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Level\n"
"| Message\n"
"\n"
"| Warning\n"
"| “Low battery state of charge because the battery cannot be charged by the inverter. Without charging, the battery will soon switch off to protect itself.”\n"
"| Fault\n"
"| “Low state of charge. The battery will soon switch off to protect itself.”\n"
"| Fault\n"
"| “Battery was switched off due to too low a state of charge. Please contact your installer.”\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Startup, updates, extension"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-startup-updates-extension
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The battery is switched on at startup via a relay (`+io0/Relay4+`, with "
"control computer CM4S Gen3 `+io0/Relay6+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-startup-updates-extension
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS contains a function to update the battery **firmware**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-startup-updates-extension
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Extending the battery:** An auxiliary function (“Prepare Battery "
"Extension”) brings the storage to a suitable state of charge before "
"installing further modules."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-startup-updates-extension
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"**Measuring the state of health (SoH):** An optional function (“SoH Cycle”) "
"carries out a charge/discharge cycle and uses it to determine the state of "
"health of the battery."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inverter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control by OpenEMS"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-by-openems
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "The inverter can be operated in three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mode\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| SMART (default)\n"
"| The inverter controls itself (fast); OpenEMS switches to its own specifications when required, e.g. for price control or grid charging.\n"
"| INTERNAL\n"
"| Only the internal control of the inverter; no specifications from OpenEMS.\n"
"| REMOTE\n"
"| OpenEMS specifies everything. Slower, but possible without a smart meter at the grid connection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grid regulations"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-grid-regulations
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The inverter component contains extensive settings for the grid connection "
"rules, including grid code (VDE-AR-N 4105 / 4110), power reduction at over- "
"and underfrequency (P(F)), power depending on voltage (P(U)) and reactive "
"power methods (fixed cos φ, cos φ(P), Q(U), Q(P)). The installer sets these "
"values according to the specifications of the grid operator."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-emergency-power-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The **emergency power output** can be switched on or off (“Off-Grid outlet”)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-emergency-power-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"A separate meter (`+meter2+`) measures the power at the emergency power "
"output."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-emergency-power-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"In island mode, OpenEMS shows the grid state “Off-Grid” and counts the time "
"in island mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "DC surplus"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-dc-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"If the PV modules on the inverter supply more than the house and battery can "
"absorb (e.g. battery full), the “Surplus-Feed-To-Grid” function ensures that "
"this DC surplus is fed into the grid and not curtailed, provided the feed-in "
"limit allows it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Status LED"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-status-led
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS controls a status LED (component “System FENECON Home”, "
"`+system0+`). It is set up automatically by the apps for **Home 6, Home 10 "
"Gen2, Home 15, Home 20 and Home 30**, and also by the Commercial systems. "
"**On the Home 10 (Gen 1), the app does not set up a status LED.** A further "
"prerequisite is a control computer with its own switching outputs (CM3, CM4, "
"CM4S, CM4S Gen2 or Gen3). Only an admin can set up the LED app manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-status-led
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid "The LED shows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| LED\n"
"| Meaning (according to the code)\n"
"\n"
"| blue, continuous\n"
"| no fault and no warning\n"
"| blue, flashing (1 second)\n"
"| warning or fault, and no connection to the backend\n"
"| off\n"
"| warning or fault with an existing connection to the backend\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The LED also has red and green contacts; however, only blue is used for the "
"status in the current code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control computer"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-computer
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/systems/fenecon-home.adoc
msgid ""
"The FENECON Home contains a control computer based on a Raspberry Pi Compute "
"Module. The code distinguishes between CM3, CM4, CM4S, CM4S Gen2 and Gen3. "
"Some functions (e.g. status LED, § 14a limitation) depend on this hardware."
msgstr ""

